        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1b804f9d-4f01-52c6-9893-193d23f770fa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rosario Castellanos, Lucy Maud Montgomery, Jean-Claude Andro, Carlos Fuentes\n- Roles: poet, author, novelist, translator\n- Works: Anne of Green Gables, Zone sacrée, Chant des aveugles, Christ des ténèbres\n\nFacts:\n- Lucy Maud Montgomery was born on November 30, 1874, and she was a Canadian author who published as L.M. Montgomery.\n- In 1908, Lucy Maud Montgomery began the novel series for which she is best known with Anne of Green Gables.\n- Rosario Castellanos Figueroa was born on May 25, 1925, and she was a Mexican poet and author.\n- Jean-Claude Andro later pursued a career as a novelist and translator.\n- Jean-Claude Andro translated Zone sacrée and Chant des aveugles by Carlos Fuentes.\n- Jean-Claude Andro translated Christ des ténèbres by Rosario Castellanos.\n- Rosario Castellanos Figueroa died on August 7, 1974.\n- Lucy Maud Montgomery died on April 24, 1942.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "9390cb88-e1f6-51a6-aebb-e24c3911921b",
        "text": "Page: Rosario Castellanos. Sentence: Rosario Castellanos Figueroa (] ; 25 May 1925 – 7 August 1974) was a Mexican poet and author.\nPage: Lucy Maud Montgomery. Sentence: Lucy Maud Montgomery {'1': \", '2': \", '3': \", '4': \"} (November 30, 1874 – April 24, 1942) published as L.M. Montgomery, was a Canadian author best known for a series of novels beginning in 1908 with \"Anne of Green Gables\".\nPage: Jean-Claude Andro. Sentence: He then pursued a career as a novelist and translator (\"Zone sacrée\" and \"Chant des aveugles\" by Carlos Fuentes and \"Christ des ténèbres\" by Rosario Castellanos).",
